{{Quote|You hear about the hospital over in Wormstew Town?|A citizen|<ref name="Star Wars 34" />}}
'''Wormstew Town''' was a [[City|town]] on the [[Smuggler]]'s [[Moon]] of [[Nar Shaddaa]]. The [[human]] [[Sana Starros]] grew up in the town.<ref name="Star Wars 34" /> The outfit known as [[Jega's Squad]] operated out of [[Jega's Music Hall and Petting Zoo]], which was located in Wormstew Town.<ref name="4Z" /> Around [[1 ABY]],<ref name="1 Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''Star Wars'' (2015) 34 to around [[1 ABY]].</ref> a [[Wormstew Town hospital|hospital]] located in Wormstew Town was in danger of closing down. After an operation alongside the scoundrel [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] that left Starros with thousands of [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] in profit, Starros anonymously left a dozen sacks of credits on the hospital's doorsteps.<ref name="Star Wars 34" /> In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="3 Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Star Wars: War of the Bounty Hunters]]'', which includes ''War of the Bounty Hunters &ndash; 4-LOM & Zuckuss'' 1, to [[3 ABY]].</ref> the [[Gand]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Zuckuss]] stumbled into Jega's Music Hall and Petting Zoo, encountering the [[Lurmen]] [[Trot]] there before ultimately battling his usual companion [[4-LOM]] in the streets of Wormstew Town. Zuckuss would be assisted by Jega's Squad in the fight.<ref name="4Z" />

==Behind the scenes==
Wormstew Town was first mentioned in ''Star Wars'' 34,<ref name="Star Wars 34" /> the [[Star Wars (2015) 34|thirty-fourth issue]] of the [[Star Wars comic books|comic book]] series [[Star Wars (2015)|''Star Wars'']]. It was written by [[Jason Aaron]], illustrated by [[Salvador Larroca]], and published by [[Marvel Comics]] on [[August 16]], [[2017]]<ref name="Newsarama">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/60817/star_wars_2015_34|text=Star Wars (2015) #34}}</ref> before appearing in [[War of the Bounty Hunters – 4-LOM & Zuckuss 1|''War of the Bounty Hunters – 4-LOM & Zuckuss'' 1]],<ref name="4Z" /> a one-shot comic issue within the crossover event ''[[Star Wars: War of the Bounty Hunters]]'' written by [[Daniel José Older]], illustrated by [[Kei Zama]] and [[Felipe Sobreiro]], and published by Marvel Comics on [[August 4]], [[2021]].<ref name="Marvel 2">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/93560/star_wars_war_of_the_bounty_hunters_-_4-lom_zuckuss_2021_1|text=Star Wars: War of the Bounty Hunters &ndash; 4-Lom & Zuckuss (2021) #1}}</ref>

